IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lta-landtax`
IMPORT `lta-qa`

-- Land Tax Assessment Act 2002 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (lta-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading a BOOLEAN or NUMBER input that is ASSUMEd stops the evaluation
-- with an error. Each question with a situation input is asked, for its role, with the situation FALSE and every later
-- input ASSUMEd. Those two groups are generated from the parameter lists (scratchpad qa_params.py) and come last. The
-- hand-worked cases come first: each answer is worked by hand from the deposited text, and for the owner (the
-- baseline's seat) each question is also asserted equal to the baseline export's answer on the same facts. Life facts:
-- Chloe c055, Daniel d055 and d084, as in lta-cases-landtax.l4; every other fixture is HYPOTHETICAL. A day is
-- YYYYMMDD; a financial year is named by the year in which it ends.
--
-- `Who owns it` is read by the baseline through a CONSIDER that lists every value, with no OTHERWISE, so an ASSUMEd
-- value fails if read. The list of lots is read by CONSIDER on the list.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked Who owns it` IS A `Who owns it`
ASSUME `an unasked list of Lot` IS A LIST OF `Lot`

`as the owner` MEANS `I own the land, or the home I live in`
`as the holder` MEANS `I hold land for someone else, as their agent, a trustee, or an executor or administrator`
`as the occupier` MEANS `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns`

`d055, Nedlands at 30 June 2038, as a record` MEANS `My position at the taxing date` WITH
    `I was the owner` IS TRUE
    `there was an agreement for the sale of the land` IS FALSE
    `I was the seller under the agreement` IS FALSE
    `I was the buyer under the agreement` IS FALSE
    `the buyer had obtained possession` IS FALSE

`d084, the Nedlands house at 30 June 2063, as a record` MEANS `My home at the taxing date` WITH
    `has a building occupied or fit and intended to be occupied as a residence` IS TRUE
    `the building is a hotel, motel, hostel, lodging or boarding house or ordinarily holiday accommodation` IS FALSE
    `is held in trust` IS FALSE
    `owned by` IS `spouses`
    `an owner uses it as their primary residence` IS TRUE
    `every owner who does not live there is an owner only as a guarantor a lender required` IS TRUE
    `percentage owned by the owners who live there` IS 100

`half each with a sibling living elsewhere, as a record` MEANS `My home at the taxing date` WITH
    `has a building occupied or fit and intended to be occupied as a residence` IS TRUE
    `the building is a hotel, motel, hostel, lodging or boarding house or ordinarily holiday accommodation` IS FALSE
    `is held in trust` IS FALSE
    `owned by` IS `two or more other individuals`
    `an owner uses it as their primary residence` IS TRUE
    `every owner who does not live there is an owner only as a guarantor a lender required` IS FALSE
    `percentage owned by the owners who live there` IS 50

`c055, the Byford build, as a record` MEANS `My new home being built` WITH
    `is held in trust` IS FALSE
    `day I became owner of the land` IS 20280515
    `commencement day` IS 20280220
    `completion day` IS 20290715
    `I am the first occupant` IS TRUE
    `I use it as my primary residence in the year it is completed` IS TRUE
    `income was derived from the property before I first occupied it` IS FALSE
    `another home of mine is exempt as my primary residence for the year` IS FALSE

`d055, both homes at 30 June 2038, as a record` MEANS `My two homes` WITH
    `I owned both at the taxing date` IS TRUE
    `the home I lived in at the taxing date is exempt for the year` IS TRUE
    `the other home would have been exempt had I lived there instead` IS TRUE
    `I acquired the second home in the previous financial year` IS TRUE
    `I lived in the other home before the previous one in that year or after it in the assessment year` IS TRUE
    `I sold and handed over the home I acquired first during the assessment year` IS TRUE
    `income was derived from the home not lived in while I owned both` IS FALSE

`in aged care, the house empty, as a record` MEANS `My home while I am in care` WITH
    `is held in trust` IS FALSE
    `owned at the taxing date by me alone, with my spouse or partner, or with guarantors only` IS TRUE
    `I am in full-time care at the taxing date` IS TRUE
    `just before my care began I so owned it and lived in it as my primary residence` IS TRUE
    `income was derived from it in the relevant period` IS FALSE
    `another property of mine is exempt as my primary residence` IS FALSE

`death in March 2069, the house empty, as a record` MEANS `My home after my death` WITH
    `the financial year of my death` IS 2069
    `my ownership and use gave or would have given a s 21 or s 26B exemption that year` IS TRUE
    `my executor owns it at midnight on 30 June of the year of death` IS TRUE
    `my estate derives rent or income from it before the end of the assessment year` IS FALSE

`a rental unit at 650000` MEANS `Lot` WITH
    `taxable value` IS 650000
    `percentage exempt` IS 0

`a vacant block at 400000` MEANS `Lot` WITH
    `taxable value` IS 400000
    `percentage exempt` IS 0

§§ `For the owner`

-- The financial year and the taxing date (s 7(1)): 15 July 2029 is in 2029/30; land tax for 2063/64 is fixed at
-- midnight on 30 June 2063 (d084).
#ASSERT `Which financial year is this day in` `as the owner` 20290715 EQUALS `the financial year ending 30 June` 2030
#ASSERT `Which financial year is this day in` `as the owner` 20380520 EQUALS `the financial year ending 30 June` (`In which financial year does this day fall` 20380520)
#ASSERT `On which day is my land tax fixed` `as the owner` 2064 EQUALS `the day` 20630630
#ASSERT `On which day is my land tax fixed` `as the owner` 2039 EQUALS `the day` (`At midnight on which day is my land tax fixed` 2039)
-- ss 7(1), 8(3), d055: owner at 30 June 2038, liable; the seller whose buyer had possession, not; the seller whose buyer
-- had not, liable; the buyer without possession, not.
#ASSERT `Am I the one liable for the land tax` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I the one liable for the land tax` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I the one liable for the land tax` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I the one liable for the land tax` `as the owner` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I the one liable for the land tax` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I liable for the land tax on this land` `d055, Nedlands at 30 June 2038, as a record`)
-- s 7(4): every joint owner can be made to pay the whole; s 12(3): joint land is a separate assessment.
#ASSERT `Can I be made to pay all the tax on my joint land` `as the owner` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I be made to pay all the tax on my joint land` `as the owner` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can I be made to pay all the land tax on land I own jointly` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is my joint land assessed with the land I own alone` `as the owner` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my joint land assessed with the land I own alone` `as the owner` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` `Is my joint land assessed with my own land`
-- Glossary cl 1: a house lived in is private residential property; a beach house ordinarily used for holidays is not;
-- a vacant block is not.
#ASSERT `Is my lot private residential property` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my lot private residential property` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my lot private residential property` `as the owner` FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my lot private residential property` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my land private residential property` `d084, the Nedlands house at 30 June 2063, as a record`)
-- s 21: d084, spouses living there, wholly exempt; held in trust, not; a company, not; half each with a sibling living
